#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Download and flash Arch Linux ARM to an SD card for Raspberry Pi.

Creates a bootable SD card with:
- Partitioned and formatted card (boot: FAT32, root: ext4)
- Dotfiles installed for both root and a named user
- SSH daemon enabled with required authorized keys

Supports Raspberry Pi models 2-5 via --model (default: 5). Models 3-5 use
the AArch64 image, model 2 the ARMv7 image. The stock AArch64 image boots
via U-Boot and a mainline kernel, which does not support the Pi 5 — for
model 5 the boot partition is rebuilt with the Raspberry Pi foundation
kernel (linux-rpi-16k) instead.

Supports resuming after failure — completed steps are tracked on the
target filesystem and skipped on re-run.
"""

